Subject: Makes register stores non-owning under deferred RC

What this does
  Makes register stores non-owning under deferred RC.

Why we need it
  With registers published as roots, a zero-count table and exact-count fixes, the dup on every register write and the old-value release test on every overwrite are pure overhead: a value a register still sees is parked rather than freed, so registers can borrow.

What it adds
  Register writes no longer dup/release; stores from a register into an owning home (locals, `regvm_put_arg`, object fill, return to C, catch unwind, for-of wrappers) dup; a suspended coroutine's window owns while parked (`rv_owns_regs`, `js_regvm_drc_suspend`/`_resume`, initial yield included) and `async_func_mark`/`async_func_free` walk it only then; `arg_owned` includes `JS_CALL_FLAG_GENERATOR` (a coroutine's heap `arg_buf` is owned though resumed with `argv == arg_buf`); record calls borrow the caller's argument window only when `regvm_args_borrowable` (new `JSFunctionBytecode.args_captured`, no mapped `arguments`/`make_arg_ref`); `__JS_FreeAtom` parks a zero-count atom with `js_drc_zero` and `JS_FreeAtomStruct` turns a parked atom back into a plain string so the deferred free does not unlink it from the atom table twice; `JS_FreeRuntime` frees immediately after its final drain.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
